/target

# Library crate: Cargo.lock is not checked in (see Cargo book guidance for
# libraries). CI generates its own lockfile per run.
/Cargo.lock

# Claude Code local config (not part of the published project)
.claude/

# IDEs and editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# TEST files: contains personal information, do not commit (added 2026-08-18 13:37 JST)
tests/fixtures/other

# Throwaway proof-of-concept code (design exploration, not meant to be
# merged) — see e.g. Issue #67's grouped-image transform PoC. The folder's
# own README (rules for this directory) stays tracked; everything else
# under it does not.
#
# Pattern must match the actual on-disk directory name (`poc/`, lowercase)
# exactly — git's gitignore matching is case-sensitive regardless of the
# filesystem, so a case mismatch here (previously `/PoC/*`) silently stops
# ignoring anything on a case-sensitive filesystem (Linux/CI), even though
# it appears to work locally on macOS's default case-insensitive one.
/poc/*
!/poc/README.md

# scripts/generate_real_fixtures.py's own bytecode cache.
scripts/__pycache__/
